 MANY model. Both will be cognizant of the JOIN model, however. This is a rare scenario. Let\u2019s use a bizarre, somewhat contrived, and controversial example. Let\u2019s say we have a ONE side model, God. The MANY side model would be Human. Each God could have MANY Humans following him/her through a JOIN model of GuardianAngel. The God model could have many GuardianAngels but lets say s/he doesn\u2019t care about keeping track of all his/her follower Humans. Who said DB associations were boring?","topics":[],"score":183300,"global_rank":388711},{"name":"nglasgow/Travel_Insight","owner":"nglasgow","html_url":"https://github.com/nglasgow/Travel_Insight","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":183300,"global_rank":388712},{"name":"jdlehman/bowling_scorer","owner":"jdlehman","html_url":"https://github.com/jdlehman/bowling_scorer","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"given a formatted string, scores a bowling game","topics":[],"score":183300,"global_rank":388713},{"name":"sprestage/kitchen","owner":"sprestage","html_url":"https://github.com/sprestage/kitchen","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"Kitchen application tracks your recipes and ingredients.","topics":[],"score":183300,"global_rank":388715},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":183300,"global_rank":388716},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":183300,"global_rank":388717},{"name":"justinfaulkner/mog_simulator","owner":"justinfaulkner","html_url":"https://github.com/justinfaulkner/mog_simulator","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"lan